  "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.9600)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.9600)=1-0.975=0.025.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-1.9600)=0.025.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/8a3513b66e17745585f5f49ea3cb1b1c7241874159e3cfaca0e5f644d0b7a3c2.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-1.9600) & =0.025 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.9600) & =0.025.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.9600.$",
